From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:40:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] build: write each job's output whole to a package's log

A package built in parallel runs its jobs beside each other, and each
compiler writes its diagnostics to the package's log as it goes. A
diagnostic is written in pieces, its "In function" context and its chain
of inlined calls apart from the message itself, so the pieces of jobs
running at once interleave: a warning then follows another job's
context, and a reader of the log places it in the wrong function or in
none.

Run a parallel package's make with --output-sync=target, which writes
each job's output once the job ends. The jobs still run in parallel,
under the build's jobserver; only their output is held back. Make passes
the option on to the makes it starts, among them the one GCC runs for a
link's LTO jobs.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 include/package.mk | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/package.mk b/include/package.mk
index 823a055..c71a75b 100644
--- a/include/package.mk
+++ b/include/package.mk
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ PKG_SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH = $(if $(DUMP),,$(call source_date_epoch,$(if \
 ifeq ($(strip $(PKG_BUILD_PARALLEL)),0)
 PKG_JOBS?=-j1
 else
-PKG_JOBS?=$(if $(PKG_BUILD_PARALLEL),$(MAKE_J),-j1)
+PKG_JOBS?=$(if $(PKG_BUILD_PARALLEL),$(MAKE_J) --output-sync=target,-j1)
 endif
 
 PKG_BUILD_FLAGS?=
